# Confluence to Azure DevOps Wiki Migration Configuration
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your actual values

# =============================================================================
# CONFLUENCE CONFIGURATION
# =============================================================================
CONFLUENCE_BASE_URL=https://yourcompany.atlassian.net
CONFLUENCE_USERNAME=your.email@company.com
CONFLUENCE_API_TOKEN=your_confluence_api_token_here
CONFLUENCE_SPACE_KEY=YOURSPACE

# =============================================================================
# AZURE DEVOPS CONFIGURATION
# =============================================================================
DEVOPS_ORGANIZATION=your-organization
DEVOPS_PROJECT=your-project
DEVOPS_WIKI_IDENTIFIER=your-project.wiki
DEVOPS_PAT=your_azure_devops_pat_token_here

# =============================================================================
# PROXY CONFIGURATION
# =============================================================================
# Choose ONE of the following proxy configurations:

# Option 1: PAC Proxy (Proxy Auto-Configuration)
# Uncomment and configure the following line for PAC proxy:
# PROXY_PAC_URL=http://webproxy.francotyp.com:8080/proxy.pac

# Option 2: Normal HTTP/HTTPS Proxy
# Uncomment and configure the following lines for normal proxy:
# HTTP_PROXY=http://proxy.company.com:8080
# HTTPS_PROXY=http://proxy.company.com:8080
# 
# Optional: If you need different proxies for HTTP and HTTPS:
# HTTP_PROXY=http://http-proxy.company.com:8080
# HTTPS_PROXY=http://https-proxy.company.com:8080

# Option 3: SOCKS Proxy
# Uncomment and configure the following line for SOCKS proxy:
# SOCKS_PROXY=socks5://proxy.company.com:1080

# Option 4: No Proxy (Direct Connection)
# Uncomment the following line to explicitly disable proxy:
# NO_PROXY=true

# =============================================================================
# PROXY AUTHENTICATION (if required)
# =============================================================================
# If your proxy requires authentication, add these:
# PROXY_USERNAME=your_proxy_username
# PROXY_PASSWORD=your_proxy_password

# =============================================================================
# ADVANCED PROXY CONFIGURATION
# =============================================================================
# You can also set these standard environment variables:
# http_proxy=http://proxy.company.com:8080
# https_proxy=http://proxy.company.com:8080
# no_proxy=localhost,127.0.0.1,.local

# =============================================================================
# NOTES
# =============================================================================
# 1. The migration tool will automatically detect proxy configuration from
#    environment variables in this order:
#    - PROXY_PAC_URL (for PAC proxy)
#    - HTTP_PROXY/HTTPS_PROXY (for normal proxy)
#    - NO_PROXY (for no proxy)
#    - Default to no proxy if none are set
#
# 2. For PAC proxy, make sure the pypac library is installed:
#    pip install pypac
#
# 3. For SOCKS proxy, make sure the requests[socks] library is installed:
#    pip install requests[socks]
#
# 4. The tool will test the connection after configuration and show your
#    external IP address to verify proxy is working correctly.
